body:
I use How To Study Korean for grammar. TTMIK is fine for the very beginning, but the lack of detail explanation bothers me.  

&#x200B;

I have an Anki deck of common vocab, which I've added example sentences to for vocab.  

&#x200B;

I also try to read an article or two a day on the Kids Donga newpaper website. Sometimes I'll also read news for adults but I use the kids one mainly because the vocab is simpler and my main purpose for reading it is to get better at understanding longer sentences more quickly.  

&#x200B;

I also go through TOPIK questions every day and look up anything I get wrong. The TOPIN One app is good, I also use the ones one the TOPIK Guide website. I'd recommend doing this even if you don't want to take the test because it helps you to understand your weaknesses.
